; ==== the engine (T4): names and what the code shows
; Checked by running (tools/run.py) where it says so; the rest is read
; from the code. "Presumably" marks a guess.

; ---- start-up and the game states
name CODE:0000 start
comment CODE:0000 start: memory, the table number from the command line, mode 13h, INT 9, options, high scores
name CODE:0089 main_loop
comment CODE:0089 calls the routine of the game state [game_state] (state_table), for ever
name DATA:8188 state_table
name DATA:8A8A game_state
comment DATA:8A8A the game state, an index into state_table (checked: 1 at start, 2 idle, 3 ball start, 5 playing, 6 ball lost)
name DATA:971A table_num
comment DATA:971A the table, 0-3, the digit on the command line (checked)
name CODE:4F39 st_quit
comment CODE:4F39 state 0: saves the high scores, then state 10
name CODE:009F st_load
comment CODE:009F state 1: loads the table (files, set-up, lights, screen, palette) and the sound driver, then state 2
name CODE:00EB st_idle
comment CODE:00EB state 2: no game; the display and the table scroll up and down; F1-F8 start a game for 1-8 players, Esc asks to quit
name CODE:016A idle_loop
comment CODE:016A state 2's loop, a frame each (read_game_keys to idle_show)
name CODE:01BD game_scroll_down
comment CODE:01BD scrolls the table down to its end, then state 3 (also where a new game from the game over state goes on)
name CODE:04E6 st_ball_start
comment CODE:04E6 state 3: a new ball for the current player: the ball to the plunger, "player n" on the display for 46h frames, then plays until the ball leaves the plunger lane (x < [lane_exit_x]), then state 5
name CODE:04EE ball_start
name CODE:0553 ball_start_loop
name CODE:041F st_ball_locked
comment CODE:041F state 4: a ball was locked (lock_ball): a new ball to the plunger, the table scrolls down, then as state 3 (seen running in the 350-line mode, entered by writing game_state; a lock by play not seen)
comment CODE:041F its scroll loop (from CODE:04B4) tests the 320x200 mode's end (29E000h) and then falls into the 350-line mode's test (a JMP presumably missing, as game_scroll_down has one), which subtracts 172000h from what is left: with scroll_step keeping the scroll at 29E000h at most that is always below 0, so in the 320x200 mode the loop does not end (checked by running with game_state set to 4 at st_play: scroll stays at 29E000h, a pass a picture, since set_screen_start waits for the retrace)
name CODE:04B4 ball_locked_loop
name CODE:0653 st_play
comment CODE:0653 state 5: the game: scroll, ball, nudge, plunger, the table's logic, drawing; ball drained: state 6; Esc: state 2
name CODE:15F4 st_ball_lost
comment CODE:15F4 state 6: the ball is lost: scrolls down, bonus (times the multiplier) and boosters counted into the score, then the next player (state 3), or a locked ball back into play (state 5), or game over (state 7)
name CODE:16AF ball_lost_count
comment CODE:16AF after a drained ball: "ball lost" for 46h frames, then (unless tilted) count_bonus, "bonus held", count_boosters
name CODE:1736 count_boosters
comment CODE:1736 the player's boosters (player record +10h, BCD) one by one: shown in td_txt_boosters, add_booster, minus booster_step
name CODE:17A5 next_player
comment CODE:17A5 extra_ball: the same player again; else the next player, after the last one the next ball (ball_num), after the last ball game over (state 7)
name CODE:17EE release_locked_ball
comment CODE:17EE a ball is locked: the first lock of td_locks puts its ball back into play (position and speed from the lock's object), state 5
name CODE:1883 st_game_over
comment CODE:1883 state 7: high score entry for each player, then the scores in turn; F1-F8 start a new game, else state 2
name DATA:8A89 over_last
comment DATA:8A89 st_game_over: last_player as the game ended; over_player (8A87h) counts the players down from it + 1, over_rounds (8A85h) the four rounds of showing their scores
name DATA:8A87 over_player
name DATA:8A85 over_rounds
name DATA:89AC hiscore_jingled
comment DATA:89AC FFh once the high score jingle (28h) has played in this game over
name CODE:1338 st_pause
comment CODE:1338 state 8 (key P): the music paused, "game paused"; Esc asks to quit, any other key goes on (state 5)
name CODE:12CD st_tilt
comment CODE:12CD state 9: tilt: flippers off, the ball's bonus cleared, "tilt" until the ball drains, then state 6
name CODE:1A34 st_exit
comment CODE:1A34 state 10: INT 9 back, palette black, video memory cleared, exit to DOS
name CODE:1A2D st_restart
comment CODE:1A2D states 11, 13-15: state 1 again
name CODE:4C91 st_12
name DATA:661F msg_player1_score
comment DATA:661F st_12: a message whose text gets player 1's score at +24h
name DATA:78D4 txt_game_over2
comment CODE:4C91 state 12: player 1's score in a text, then state 11; nothing sets state 12 (left over, presumably)
name CODE:0FA3 fatal_error
comment CODE:0FA3 a file could not be loaded: sound off, text mode, the error text, exit
name CODE:4CEE parse_cmdline
comment CODE:4CEE BX = PSP: the first digit of the command line minus '0' into BL; CF when there is none
name CODE:0FBF print_at
comment CODE:0FBF not called: the DOS text at DS:DX ('$' at its end) at the cursor CX (column, row), the cursor read back after it
name CODE:0FD0 set_cursor
comment CODE:0FD0 the BIOS cursor to cursor_col/cursor_row on cursor_page
name CODE:0FE1 get_cursor
name DATA:96DC cursor_col
name DATA:96DD cursor_row
name DATA:96DE cursor_page
name CODE:009C exit_jump
comment CODE:009C not reached: a jump to st_exit
name CODE:4D1B dos_alloc
comment CODE:4D1B AX paragraphs -> AX = segment (CF on failure)
name CODE:4D28 dos_free
name CODE:4D33 dos_resize
comment CODE:4D33 not called
name CODE:4E23 load_file
comment CODE:4E23 the file named at DS:DX into ES:DI, 32 KB at a time; CF on failure
name CODE:4D9F load_options
comment CODE:4D9F C:\DELUXE\DDPCOPTN.BIN into the options (9A96h), or the defaults when it is missing; opt_balls 1 becomes 3 balls, else 5
name CODE:277E load_hiscores
comment CODE:277E C:\DELUXE\HISCORES.PD1 into hiscores, or the defaults (hiscores_default) when it is missing
name CODE:275E save_hiscores
name CODE:27AC write_file
name DATA:96E1 file_handle
name DATA:96E3 file_size
comment CODE:27AC creates the file DS:DX and writes [96E3h] bytes from DI (DS = AX)

; ---- the per-table set-up
name CODE:0691 load_table_files
comment CODE:0691 TBLDETLO.xxx (collision map, lower level) to BSS:0960, TBLDETHI.xxx (upper level, not for Ignition) to BSS:47E0, TABLE2M.xxx (the picture) to a new block ([table_pic_seg])
name CODE:0710 table_setup
comment CODE:0710 the ball, plunger and two unused object records, the table's own set-up, the flipper sprites' first frames
name CODE:0788 setup_ignition
comment CODE:0788 fills the table descriptor (8494h..84E0h) and the table's constants; the same for the other three
name CODE:08EC setup_steel_wheel
name CODE:0A50 setup_beat_box
name CODE:0BBA setup_nightmare
name CODE:0D0C place_flipper_shapes
comment CODE:0D0C each shape record of flipper_shape_data: x := [flipper_x], y from the list at SI (a word per frame)
name CODE:4BE3 table_check
comment CODE:4BE3 does nothing (called by each table's set-up; see machine_check)
name CODE:4BE5 machine_check
comment CODE:4BE5 not called: compares machine_checksum with the one stored at 8440h (a copy protection taken out, presumably)
name CODE:4C26 machine_checksum
comment CODE:4C26 a sum of the BIOS ROM, the free space of the current drive and the first hard disk's parameters (INT 41h vector)
name CODE:0E2C init_lights
comment CODE:0E2C gives each light record its palette slot (+22h) and copies the lights' "off" colours into light_palette
name CODE:108F setup_screen
comment CODE:108F the screen mode (opt_screen), the table picture into video memory, FLIPPERS.SPR loaded and made into sprite shapes, the split screen for the display
name CODE:0D35 new_game
comment CODE:0D35 clears the eight players' records and the jackpots; player 1; balls from the options; random seed from the frame counter

; ---- one frame of play
name CODE:021C read_game_keys
comment CODE:021C F1-F8: number of players - 1 into last_player; Esc: quit_request
name CODE:02A6 ask_quit
comment CODE:02A6 "really quit <y/n>": CF when Y
name CODE:02D7 idle_show
comment CODE:02D7 state 2's show: the texts of td_idle_texts, the table scrolling up and down (idle_scroll)
name CODE:039A scroll_toward
comment CODE:039A one scroll step toward the line [89BBh]/8
name CODE:03D8 idle_scroll
comment CODE:03D8 one scroll step down to the end, then up to the top ([89BDh] the direction)
name DATA:89BD idle_dir
comment DATA:89BD idle_scroll's direction: 0 down, FFh up
name DATA:8AC3 idle_text
comment DATA:8AC3 idle_show: the entry of td_idle_texts (a list of messages, a negative word at its end) shown now
name DATA:89B9 tour_on
comment DATA:89B9 Ignition's idle show: FFh while it goes through td_idle_scroll (after the idle texts), 0 while the texts run
name DATA:8AC5 tour_step
comment DATA:8AC5 the entry of td_idle_scroll shown now: 6 bytes, a message, a light group (into tour_lamps), the line to scroll to (tour_line); a negative word after the last
name DATA:89BA tour_wait
comment DATA:89BA frames (10h) the table scrolls toward the next step's line before its message starts
name DATA:89BB tour_line
comment DATA:89BB the line idle_show scrolls toward (scroll_toward: the scroll's high word is this / 8)
name DATA:657D tour_lamps
comment DATA:657D a list of one light group (and FFFFh), the tour step's: idle_update_lights shows its lamps' blink phases
name CODE:05BE show_player_up
comment CODE:05BE during the ball start: "player n" / the players and the ball number, blinking
name DATA:8CDF player_blink_timer
comment DATA:8CDF show_player_up: frames (14h) until the current player's digit changes (player_blink); st_idle sets 1
name DATA:8CDE player_blink
name DATA:8AA1 wait_count
comment DATA:8AA1 frames of a counted wait: ball_start's "player n" (46h), the bonus count (bonus_count_step)
name DATA:6676 txt_shoot_player
comment DATA:6676 show_player_up's text for a ball after a lock, the player's digit written at +13h
name DATA:8A9F bonus_count_period
comment DATA:8A9F bonus_count_step: frames between two steps of the count (4)
name DATA:8CC6 score_copy
comment DATA:8CC6 score_to_best: the current player's score (8 bytes) compared with the others'; run_event clears its first word
name DATA:8A9B unused_8A9B
comment DATA:8A9B reset_ball_objects clears it, nothing reads it (as far as the code shows)
name DATA:8A9E unused_8A9E
comment DATA:8A9E reset_ball_objects clears it, nothing reads it (as far as the code shows)
name DATA:9718 unused_9718
comment DATA:9718 new_game writes frame_count's low byte here and its complement at 9719h, nothing reads them (as far as the code shows)
name DATA:9719 unused_9719
name DATA:0E20 ball_event_1
comment DATA:0E20 table_ball_events: the sequence run at every new ball on table 1, ball_event_3 (and object ball_object_3 disarmed) on table 3; game_object_3 armed for all at a new game on table 3 (table_game_objects)
name DATA:29D0 ball_event_3
name DATA:2DCC ball_object_3
name DATA:30A6 game_object_3
name CODE:0FF2 reset_ball
comment CODE:0FF2 the ball to its start (ball_start_x/y), speed 0, gravity from opt_slope, flippers on, the table's objects for a new ball
name CODE:2830 reset_ball_objects
comment CODE:2830 the ball to its start, and the per-ball state: locks, bonus (unless held), multiplier 1, the event stack, the lower level's lists
name CODE:1164 ball_frame
comment CODE:1164 key P: state 8; three ball_step; the ball's position into its object and sprite; below line 512: ball_drained
name CODE:1233 nudge
comment CODE:1233 the nudge key shakes the table (nudge_phase, nudge_push); more than three nudges within 46h frames: tilt (state 9) (checked: the key; the tilt not)
name CODE:1387 plunger
comment CODE:1387 key held: plunger_pull counts to 20h, the plunger sprite moves down; let go: the ball in the lane gets a speed of -pull*80h (checked)
name CODE:141B scroll_follow
comment CODE:141B the scroll speed from the ball's height on the screen (a dead zone of 12h lines around line 37h)
name CODE:1467 scroll_step
comment CODE:1467 scroll += scroll_speed, kept within the table; the CRTC start address from it (nudge_phase shakes it by a line)
name CODE:15DD set_screen_start
comment CODE:15DD the CRTC start address [screen_start], then wait_frame
name CODE:14F9 play_frame
name CODE:156F play_after_holes
comment CODE:156F where play_frame goes on after map_event_run; for an event number whose map_events entry is 0, map_event_run pops this return address, compares the holes with it (clearing the others' busy bytes, and DATA:0001 for the 0 entries) and returns from play_frame (read, not checked by running)
comment CODE:14F9 the table's logic for a frame: texts, timers, the hit rectangles and lanes, the map's events, the event stack, drawing, the groups of lights
name CODE:2BC3 lights_frame
comment CODE:2BC3 the lights for a frame: blinking, the current player's lights into the palette, Ignition's timers, the light chains
name CODE:2BD2 idle_lights
name CODE:159E copy_to_vram
comment CODE:159E CX bytes of a picture (4 planes interleaved, segment AX) into video memory at DI, plane by plane

; ---- keyboard
name CODE:2AC0 hook_int9
name CODE:2AE5 unhook_int9
name CODE:2AFB kbd_int
comment CODE:2AFB INT 9: key_map bit n = scancode n down; E0-prefixed keys + 80h, the E0 shifts dropped (checked)
name CODE:2B58 wait_keys_up
comment CODE:2B58 until no key is down
name CODE:2B73 wait_key_down
comment CODE:2B73 until a key is down (not called)
name DATA:96BC key_map
comment DATA:96BC 256 bits: bit n = scancode n is down; tested as byte index + mask, the words of the options
name DATA:82AA old_int9
name CODE:2B57 kbd_e0
comment CODE:2B57 an E0 prefix came

; ---- the ball
name CODE:1F02 ball_step
comment CODE:1F02 one physics step (three a frame): the flippers swept against the ball, the ball moved through the collision map pixel by pixel (bounces), position += speed, then flippers and gravity
name CODE:1EB8 ball_step_size
comment CODE:1EB8 the step's pixels in x and y and their directions (977Eh..9781h)
name CODE:1BF4 ball_collide
comment CODE:1BF4 the ball's next pixel against the collision map (map_test) and the flippers' shapes; CF and the surface when it hits
name CODE:1B8F map_test
comment CODE:1B8F the collision map at x = CX, y = DX (0..511): CF and AL = the surface, DH = its angle when the pixel is one of the row's surface pixels, else CF clear
comment CODE:1B8F TBLDETLO/TBLDETHI: only the pixels where there is a surface; per row (512, from the top) two halves, x < 256 and x >= 256; an empty half is the byte FFh, else n pixels as three arrays of n bytes: the surface (bit 7 set on the last, so the array ends the list; the value is the low 7 bits), the angle, x (low 8 bits). Checked: all fifteen files of DREAMS1 and DREAMS2 parse to their last byte this way
comment CODE:1B8F the surface's low nibble picks response_table's and surface_table's entry (the maps have 0, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7), high nibble 10h and 20h: kickers (score; surface_params), 30h and 40h (33h, 37h in DREAMS1's maps, 30h, 36h, 37h, 42h in DREAMS2's; pdfiles.py) are tested nowhere and act as their low nibble (read, not checked by running); low nibble Fh is no wall: 0Fh a one-way passage, 1Fh a line whose angle byte is a code or an event number (map_special)
name CODE:1A68 index_map
comment CODE:1A68 the row index at the start of BSS for the map the far pointer at BX points to (lower_map or upper_map): 512 rows of 4 bytes, +0 the offset of the row's x array of the first half, +2 the first half's pixels, +3 the second half's
name CODE:1A8D map_run
comment CODE:1A8D ES:BX = a half row: AL = its pixels (up to the byte with bit 7), 0 for FFh; BX past the surface array
name CODE:1DB3 map_special
comment CODE:1DB3 a pixel of surface xFh; CF when it is to act as a wall: 0Fh (while map_flags bit 0 is set) is a wall of type 6 when the ball comes from one side (its direction against the angle byte; the test not worked out in detail), else it is passed and bit 0 cleared; 1Fh (while bit 1 is set) gives its angle byte to map_code, the result to map_event, bit 1 cleared; others (2Fh..7Fh, none in the maps) are passed
name CODE:1E02 map_code
comment CODE:1E02 AL = the angle byte of a 1Fh pixel: FCh gravity 10h, FBh gravity 9 (seen on Beat Box), FEh up to the upper level (its map, hit rectangles and lanes, the ball drawn in front; the FEh lines are in each TBLDETLO but Ignition's), FDh back to the lower one (in each TBLDETHI; both checked: runs with random flipper keys, Steel Wheel up the left loop ramp at t=24.3 s and down at 26.4 s, ball_level FFh and hit_rects = td_rects_upper in between; Nightmare twice); AL = FFh after a code, else the value is an event number (0..0Fh in the maps, and one 80h in TBLDETHI.BBX at (82,33): not bounded, map_event_run's ADD AL,AL drops its top bit, so it is event 0; read, not checked by running; map_event)
name CODE:1E92 collision_response
comment CODE:1E92 the hit point into hit_x/hit_y, then the routine of response_table for the surface (all: bounce_response)
name CODE:2532 bounce_response
comment CODE:2532 the response of every surface: bounce, then the step sizes again; step_count becomes the smaller of what was left and the new sum
name CODE:20C9 bounce
comment CODE:20C9 the ball's speed reflected at the surface (angle [9777h]) with the surface's constants (surface_params), the flippers' and the nudge's push added
name CODE:23AF surface_params
comment CODE:23AF the five constants of the surface type from surface_table; kickers (10h, 20h) score; the flippers (types 1, 2) push with their angular speed times the distance from their pivot
name CODE:1E72 cosine
comment CODE:1E72 cosine = sine of AL+40h
name CODE:1E74 sine
comment CODE:1E74 AL = angle (80h = half a turn): the magnitude from the quarter-wave table at ES:DX (sine_table); the sign is left in CH (presumably; read, not checked)
name CODE:1EB0 load_far
comment CODE:1EB0 ES:BX := the far pointer at [BX]
name CODE:22A6 mul_fix
comment CODE:22A6 DX times the 24-bit factor at [BX] (signed), the high part into BX (presumably fixed point; read, not checked)
name CODE:2314 add_s16
comment CODE:2314 DX (CL its sign) += the signed word at [BX-1]; bounce adds the surface's speed (surface_vx/vy) and nudge_push to the ball's before the reflection and takes them off after it (quarter_sub_s16, sub_s16)
name CODE:2320 quarter_sub_s16
comment CODE:2320 DX := DX / 4 (at least 1 when DX was 1..3), then minus the signed word at [BX-1] (sub_s16)
name CODE:2335 sub_s16
name CODE:22E3 mul_u16
name CODE:22F4 mul_s16
name CODE:2341 clamp_speed
comment CODE:2341 DX (with CL as its sign) kept within -0C80h..0C80h
name CODE:2364 div_u
name CODE:239F div_s
name CODE:2471 flippers_gravity
comment CODE:2471 the flipper keys (unless flippers_off) move the flippers; the flipper sprites; gravity added to the speed; table_push decays
name CODE:24CE flipper_move
comment CODE:24CE BX = a flipper: pressed (ZF clear) speeds it up, released drops it back; angle and frame (0-10h) from the speed
name CODE:19F9 draw_flippers
comment CODE:19F9 the flipper sprites' frames from the flippers' frames
name CODE:1A45 index_flipper_shapes
comment CODE:1A45 the 17 shape pointers (flipper_shapes) into flipper_shape_data
name CODE:1AA4 flipper_sweep
comment CODE:1AA4 BX = a flipper's frame pair: steps the drawn frame toward the wanted one, testing the ball at each step
name CODE:1AC3 flipper_hit
name CODE:1AFB shape_test
comment CODE:1AFB CX = x, DX = y, BX = a flipper shape (flipper_shapes): CF clear when the point is inside
comment CODE:1AFB a flipper shape record (flipper_shape_data, DATA:4CA0h.., 17 of them): +0 bytes to the next, +2 x, +4 y (the top left, set by place_flipper_shapes), +6 the width (a byte), +8 the height (rows), +0Ah a word per row from the second on (an offset into the rows' data), then per row the columns inside (their coding not read in detail)
name DATA:9761 ball_x
comment DATA:9761 the ball's centre: x and y, 24 bits each, pixels * 400h; speed: pixels * 400h per step (checked against the screen)
name DATA:9764 ball_y
name DATA:9769 ball_vx
name DATA:976B ball_vy
name DATA:9762 ball_x_hi
name DATA:9765 ball_y_hi
name DATA:976A ball_vx_hi
name DATA:976C ball_vy_hi
name DATA:8CE1 ball_start_x
comment DATA:8CE1 where a new ball starts: dwords, pixels * 2000h (plus 7 pixels: the sprite's corner)
name DATA:8CE3 ball_start_x_hi
name DATA:8CE5 ball_start_y
name DATA:8CE7 ball_start_y_hi
name DATA:8D3C ball_obj
comment DATA:8D3C records of 26h bytes: +0 flags (1 = shown), +2 x, +6 y (dwords, pixels * 2000h), +12h, +16h the speed; the ball, the plunger (8D62h); 8CF0h and 8D16h are set up and never used
name DATA:8D62 plunger_obj
name DATA:8CF0 unused_obj1
name DATA:8D16 unused_obj2
name DATA:9767 plunger_pull
name DATA:89BF lane_exit_x
comment DATA:89BF the ball has left the plunger lane when its sprite's x is below this
name DATA:974A gravity_x
name DATA:974C gravity
comment DATA:974C added to ball_vy every step: 9 + 2 * (opt_slope - 1); the map codes FCh/FBh set 10h/9
name DATA:9776 surface
comment DATA:9776 what the ball hit: the map's surface (map_test), 1 or 2 for the left or right flipper's shape; low nibble the entry of response_table and surface_table (0 and 1 share one), high nibble 10h/20h kickers
name DATA:9777 surface_angle
comment DATA:9777 the angle of the surface hit (the map's angle byte; 100h a full turn), for bounce
name DATA:9785 hit_x
name DATA:9787 hit_y
comment DATA:9785 where the ball hit (pixels): the hit rectangles and lanes are tested with it
name DATA:81AA response_table
name DATA:81BA surface_table
comment DATA:81BA per surface type five words, copied to surface_params_v
name DATA:971D surface_params_v
name DATA:8208 kicker_score1
comment DATA:8208 score records of the kicker surfaces (types 10h and 20h), as an object's (presumably)
name DATA:8213 kicker_score2
name DATA:974E map_flags
comment DATA:974E FFh again whenever the ball's next pixel has no surface: bit 0 arms the one-way passages, bit 1 the 1Fh lines, so a line acts once per crossing (map_special)
name DATA:974F map_event
comment DATA:974F an event number from the map (FFh: none), run by map_event_run: the hole map_events[map_event]
name DATA:977E step_dx
comment DATA:977E ball_step_size: the pixels to go this step in x and y (977Fh), without sign, and their directions (+1 or FFh) at 9780h and 9781h; step_count their sum, what is left of it
name DATA:977F step_dy
name DATA:9780 step_sx
name DATA:9781 step_sy
name DATA:9782 step_count
name DATA:9783 step_err
comment DATA:9783 ball_step's line through the pixels: the next pixel is in x or y by which keeps this nearer to 0 (-step_dy after an x pixel, +step_dx after a y pixel)
name DATA:9772 phys_a
comment DATA:9772 scratch of the physics: flipper_sweep's hit (byte 1, the shape's angle byte at 9773h), ball_collide's next pixel (x here, y at 9774h), bounce's cosine (a word and a sign byte at 9774h, for mul_fix)
name DATA:9774 phys_b
name DATA:9778 phys_c
comment DATA:9778 scratch of the physics: ball_collide's count of flipper shapes missed (a byte), bounce's sine (a word and a sign byte at 977Ah)
name DATA:977A phys_c_sign
name DATA:977C bounce_along
comment DATA:977C bounce: the ball's speed along the surface (the one across it stays in DX)
name DATA:972D kick_speed
comment DATA:972D bounce: added to the speed across the surface; E4A8h at a kicker (hit_lane), F63Ch for a type 3 kicker unless the speed is already beyond FC18h, else 0
name DATA:9784 div_count
comment DATA:9784 div_u's loop counter (ends at 1)
name DATA:9734 table_push
name DATA:9727 surface_vx
comment DATA:9727 the speed of the surface hit: 0, or a flipper's at the hit point (its angular speed times the distance from the pivot; surface_params)
name DATA:9729 surface_vy
name DATA:9736 surface_type
comment DATA:9736 the surface as surface_params found it; 5: the hit rectangles are not tested (test_hit_rects)
name DATA:972B nudge_push
name DATA:9737 nudge_timer
name DATA:9738 nudge_count
name DATA:9739 nudge_key_down
name DATA:9771 nudge_phase
comment DATA:9771 0 still, 1 shaken down, 2 back up (a line on the screen each)
name DATA:89BE tilted
name DATA:8ABF ball_drained
name DATA:8A98 ball_held
comment DATA:8A98 not 0: the ball does not move (in a hole, or a lock)
name DATA:8AC0 flippers_off
name DATA:821E flipper_shape_data
comment DATA:821E far pointers: the flipper shapes, the collision maps of the lower and the upper level (BSS, from TBLDETLO/TBLDETHI), the sine table (TDATA)
name DATA:8222 lower_map
name DATA:8226 upper_map
name DATA:822A sine_table
name DATA:822E ign_flipper_ys
comment DATA:822E y of the flipper shapes per frame (17 words; Ignition's, flipper_ys the other tables'), about 1B0h..1BEh near the table's bottom
name DATA:8250 flipper_ys

; ---- the flippers
name DATA:973A lflipper
comment DATA:973A a flipper: +0 angular speed, +2 angle, +4 frame wanted, +5 frame drawn, +6 the last angle; the right one at 9742h
name DATA:973C lflipper_angle
name DATA:973E lflipper_frame_to
name DATA:973F lflipper_frame
name DATA:9740 lflipper_last
name DATA:9742 rflipper
name DATA:9744 rflipper_angle
name DATA:9746 rflipper_frame_to
name DATA:9747 rflipper_frame
name DATA:9748 rflipper_last
name DATA:8200 lflipper_pivot_x
name DATA:8202 lflipper_pivot_y
name DATA:8204 rflipper_pivot_x
name DATA:8206 rflipper_pivot_y
name DATA:975D flipper_mirror_x
comment DATA:975D the right flipper is tested with the left one's shapes at x' = flipper_mirror_x - x (ball_step)
name DATA:975F flipper_x
comment DATA:975F the x of the flipper shapes (76 to 79 by the table), the left flipper's; the right one is tested mirrored (flipper_mirror_x)
name DATA:96F5 flipper_shapes

; ---- the screen
name DATA:96EB scroll
comment DATA:96EB the table line at the top of the screen, a dword: line * 2000h; its speed in scroll_speed (checked)
name DATA:96ED scroll_hi
name DATA:96EF scroll_speed
name DATA:96F1 scroll_speed_hi
name DATA:96E5 screen_start
name DATA:96F3 frame_count
comment DATA:96F3 counts the frames of play; seeds the random choices
name DATA:9A90 sprite_seg
name DATA:9A94 table_pic_seg
name DATA:7D00 sprites
comment DATA:7D00 four sprites of 20h bytes: the ball, the left and right flipper, the plunger; +0 flags (1 shown, 2 changed, 4 drawn, 40h/80h draw_sprites' own), +1 the ball's level (80h lower, FFh upper), +2 x, +4 y (table pixels), +6 width, +8 height, +0Ah where its background is saved (video memory), +0Ch its shape (far: video memory A820h + 180h * frame for the flippers), +10h column (x/4) and +12h y where it was drawn, +14h width (columns) and +16h height drawn, +18h..+1Eh the area to redraw (columns x1, x2, lines y1, y2)
name DATA:7D01 ball_level
name DATA:7D02 sprite_x
name DATA:7D04 sprite_y
name DATA:7D80 sprite_frames
comment DATA:7D80 the table's list of flipper sprite frames (7D82h..), 10 records of 0Ah bytes: +0 x, +4 y where the frame is cut from FLIPPERS.SPR (320 pixels a line; also where it is drawn), make_sprite_shapes sets +2 (x drawn), +6 width, +8 height
name CODE:4390 draw_sprites
comment CODE:4390 the four sprites: merges overlapping areas, then per area: grab the screen into a buffer (video memory BB10h), put back old backgrounds, save new ones, draw, copy back
name CODE:44A2 sprite_area
name DATA:7CE8 area_col
comment DATA:7CE8 the area draw_sprites works on: column (x/4), line, width in columns, height; grabbed into video memory BB10h.. (area_cols bytes a line)
name DATA:7CEA area_y
name DATA:7CEC area_cols
name DATA:7CEE area_lines
name DATA:7CF0 vram_seg
comment DATA:7CF0 A000h
name CODE:452F sort_sprite_list
name CODE:4552 grab_area
comment CODE:4552 the area from the screen into video memory BB10h..
name CODE:45BA restore_backgrounds
comment CODE:45BA the sprites' old backgrounds put back into the area
name CODE:4610 save_backgrounds
comment CODE:4610 the sprites' new backgrounds saved from the area
name CODE:469F draw_sprite_shapes
comment CODE:469F the sprites drawn into the area; the ball's pixels only where the area's colour is below its level byte (80h lower, FFh upper), so the lower level's ball goes behind colours 80h.. (presumably the ramps; read, not checked)
name CODE:4794 put_area
comment CODE:4794 the area back to the screen
name CODE:47CF set_sprite_frame
comment CODE:47CF BX = frame, SI = the sprite's offset in sprites: its shape, position and size from sprite_frames
name CODE:4816 make_sprite_shapes
comment CODE:4816 the flipper frames (sprite_frames) cut from FLIPPERS.SPR into sprite shapes
name CODE:4863 make_sprite_shape
name CODE:4968 set_mode_x
comment CODE:4968 mode 13h unchained, 320x200 (opt_screen 1)
name CODE:4EC1 set_mode_350
comment CODE:4EC1 the tweaked mode for opt_screen 2: misc output A7h, CRTC table at 4F19h: 320x350 (checked)
name CODE:4E7D set_mode_e3
comment CODE:4E7D another tweaked mode (misc output E3h: 480 lines); not called
name CODE:4E57 set_mode_other
comment CODE:4E57 not called
name CODE:49C7 set_split
comment CODE:49C7 the line compare register: the display below the table as a split screen (160h, or 146h in the 350-line mode)
name CODE:49B1 black_palette
name CODE:4A10 clear_vram
name CODE:4A30 set_planes
comment CODE:4A30 DL = map mask, DH = read map
name CODE:4A47 wait_frames
comment CODE:4A47 AX frames
name CODE:4A55 wait_frame
comment CODE:4A55 until the sound driver's timer callback sets timer_tick, or (no driver) the next vertical retrace
name CODE:4A82 write_mode_0
name CODE:4A8E write_mode_1
name CODE:4B21 screen_off
name CODE:4B2D screen_on
name CODE:4B39 set_palette
comment CODE:4B39 the table's palette (ES:SI), the lights' colours at 40h.., the display's colours (grey variant with opt_palette 1)
name CODE:4D42 to_grey
comment CODE:4D42 CX RGB triples at SI into grey (30/59/11)
name CODE:4DEF grey_palettes
comment CODE:4DEF opt_palette 1: the table's and the lights' palettes made grey
name CODE:4BD8 beep
comment CODE:4BD8 not called
name CODE:54EF beep2
comment CODE:54EF not called

; ---- the display (dot matrix below the table)
name CODE:4AA0 draw_char
comment CODE:4AA0 the character DL at column [display_col] of the display (display_font, the dots through display_dots; 4 bytes of video memory a column)
name CODE:2E75 show_text
comment CODE:2E75 the text at DI (FFh at its end) on the display from column 0; returns ZF from [6581h]
name CODE:2D0B message_start
name CODE:2D13 message_step
comment CODE:2D13 one frame of a display message (DI); ZF when it has ended
comment CODE:2D13 a message: 8 bytes, +0 flags (1: scrolls in, +6 its start; 4: flashes +2 times, +3 frames each; 8: ends when the text is short (byte 12h FFh); 10h: the letters count up to theirs, then +6 frames), +1 0: to start, FFh: running, +4 the text (20 characters, FFh)
name CODE:2C27 display_frame
comment CODE:2C27 the running message (message) or, after a while without score, the next idle text of td_score_texts
name CODE:2EE3 show_score
name CODE:2EC4 show_bonus
name CODE:2ED5 show_bonus_count
name CODE:3938 update_texts
comment CODE:3938 player and ball numbers, the jackpots and the multiplier written into the table's texts
