comment DATA:971C the ball being played, from 0 (checked: counts up after the last player's ball)
name DATA:653B balls_per_game
name DATA:8A99 extra_ball
comment DATA:8A99 not 0: the player plays another ball (extra_ball_award)
name DATA:8A9C bonus_mult
name DATA:8A9A bonus_held
name DATA:8CE0 quit_request
name DATA:6537 boosters
name DATA:653D booster_value
name DATA:6539 booster_step
name DATA:89A2 score_msb
comment DATA:89A2 check_hiscore's copy of a score, high byte first, as the high score entries keep it
name DATA:654D jackpot
comment DATA:654D the jackpot (8 bytes BCD); jackpot_base its start value, jackpot_step what raise_jackpot adds (presumably; the names follow the texts)
name DATA:6545 jackpot_step
name DATA:6555 jackpot_base
name DATA:83B0 hiscores
comment DATA:83B0 per table four entries of 9 bytes: 3 letters, 6 bytes BCD
name DATA:82FD hiscores_default
name CODE:4258 bcd_add
comment CODE:4258 [DI] += [BP], 6 bytes BCD; restarts idle_timer
name CODE:429F bcd_sub
name CODE:42E3 add_booster
comment CODE:42E3 booster_value (6 bytes BCD: 00 00 00 01 00 00, a million if added at +0) added at player record +4: its 01 lands in byte +7, above the twelve digits of the score that show_score shows and check_hiscore copies; so a booster adds nothing that is seen (a bug, presumably; read, not checked by running)
name CODE:19CA check_hiscores
comment CODE:19CA each player's score through check_hiscore
name CODE:2549 check_hiscore
comment CODE:2549 SI = a player's score: into the table's high scores when high enough, with the initials entered
name CODE:2576 insert_hiscore
comment CODE:2576 score_msb into the table's four high scores (9 bytes each: initials, 6 bytes BCD from the highest) where it is higher (cmp_score), the lower ones moved down, the initials entered; a score between the second and the third takes BX = 3 with SI still at the third entry, so it overwrites the third without moving it down (a bug, presumably; read, not checked by running)
name DATA:89A8 initials
comment DATA:89A8 enter_initials: the three letters entered (blanks after Esc)
name DATA:89AB initial_index
comment DATA:89AB enter_initials: the letter shown, an index into initial_letters (0..24h)
name DATA:8285 initial_letters
name DATA:66D6 txt_hiscore_player
comment DATA:66D6 check_hiscores writes the player's digit here, in the high score entry's text
name CODE:2658 cmp_score
name CODE:267D enter_initials
comment CODE:267D the flipper keys choose a letter, the nudge key takes it (three), Esc leaves them blank
name CODE:0DF0 clear_player
name CODE:2A28 clear_players_lights
comment CODE:2A28 at a new game: the eight players' lamp bytes cleared, all lamps out, objects and sequences reset (reset_objects_all), object timers stopped, table_game_objects
name CODE:2BB3 clear_player_lights
name CODE:2F3C count_bonus
comment CODE:2F3C the bonus times the multiplier ("bonus x n"), then counted into the score digit by digit
name DATA:89AD bonus_saved
comment DATA:89AD st_ball_lost: the player's bonus (record +8, 8 bytes BCD) as it was when the ball drained, given back when the bonus is held
name DATA:8AAD bonus_left
comment DATA:8AAD count_bonus: the bonus times the multiplier (8 bytes BCD); bonus_count_step counts it down into the score
name DATA:8AA5 bonus_step
comment DATA:8AA5 bonus_count_step: what one step moves (8 bytes BCD, from bonus_unit: 1, then 10, 100 ... as the digits of bonus_left are used up)
name DATA:6582 bonus_unit
name DATA:8AA3 bonus_digits
comment DATA:8AA3 bonus_count_step: the digits of bonus_left still to count (0Fh at the start; the lowest first)
name DATA:8CBE bonus_step_ptr
comment DATA:8CBE bonus_count_step writes where its subtraction starts and ends (bonus_step, bonus_step + 6) here, and bonus_left at 8CC2h; nothing reads them (as far as the code shows)
name DATA:8CC2 bonus_left_ptr
name CODE:3F99 bonus_count_step
comment CODE:3F99 moves one step of the bonus into the score; AX = FFFFh when it is all there

; ---- lights, hit rectangles, objects, events
name DATA:8494 td_score_texts
comment DATA:8494 the table descriptor, filled by setup_*: pointers to the table's lists and texts (names from their use)
