name DATA:84DA td_txt_countdown
name DATA:84DC td_txt_boosters
name DATA:84DE td_roulette
name DATA:84E0 td_roulette_pick
name DATA:6531 hit_rects
comment DATA:6531 the lists of the ball's level (td_*_lower or td_*_upper): hit rectangles and two lists of lanes
name DATA:9754 map_events
comment DATA:9754 the table's holes by map event number (1..), set by setup_*
name DATA:6533 lanes_a
name DATA:6535 lanes_b
name DATA:9730 hit_score
name DATA:9732 hit_object
name DATA:972F hit_lane
name DATA:65A1 event_sp
comment DATA:65A1 the event stack (event_stack..): pairs (0 or FFFFh, object) pushed by run_event, run by run_events
name DATA:8AD3 event_stack
name DATA:8C53 event_sp_ball
name DATA:8AB9 running_object
name DATA:8ACC message_busy
comment DATA:8ACC FFh while a message runs (message_step), 0 after it and when the running object is done (end_running)
name DATA:8AC7 msg_starting
comment DATA:8AC7 FFh when message_start runs the message (it does not end the running object at the message's end), 0 for message_step
name DATA:8AC8 msg_period
comment DATA:8AC8 the running message's flash period (its +3), frames
name DATA:8AC9 msg_timer
comment DATA:8AC9 frames until the next flash change or count-up step
name DATA:8ACA msg_blank
comment DATA:8ACA FFh while a flashing message shows blanks
name DATA:8ACB msg_flashes
comment DATA:8ACB flashes left (the message's +2)
name DATA:8ACD msg_frame
comment DATA:8ACD frames the scrolling message has run (it moves a column every 8)
name DATA:8ACF msg_length
comment DATA:8ACF the message's +6: where a scrolling message stops, the frames a counted-up message stays
name DATA:8CB5 msg_count_max
comment DATA:8CB5 the count-up: every character shown is at most this (from '0', one more each step, until 5Ah)
name DATA:8CB6 msg_count_src
name DATA:8CD2 msg_counting
comment DATA:8CD2 FFFFh while a character of the count-up has not reached its own yet
name DATA:8CD6 msg_cols
comment DATA:8CD6 the columns left to draw (13h: the display's 20 less one)
name DATA:658C msg_count_buf
comment DATA:658C the count-up's text as far as it has counted (20 characters and FFh)
name CODE:349D end_running
comment CODE:349D running_object and message_busy cleared
name DATA:8CDA event_player_bit
name DATA:8CCE event_arm
comment DATA:8CCE run_event's word for the stack (0 fire, FFFFh arm); a scratch word of the display code as well
name DATA:8A8F ball_in_hole
comment DATA:8A8F a hole of type 6 has the ball: it stays held while messages or events run (hold_ball_check)
name DATA:8A8C lock_pending
comment DATA:8A8C a lock handler took the ball (lock_ball): held until state 4 gives a new one
name DATA:8A90 hole_period
comment DATA:8A90 a hole of type 5 has the ball: its group's points every hole_period frames (hole_timer), hole_count times, then the ball goes (add_hit_score)
name DATA:8A92 hole_timer
name DATA:8A94 hole_group
name DATA:8A96 hole_count
name DATA:8AB5 rect_clear_target
comment DATA:8AB5 the next target of a completed hit rectangle group to go out, every rect_clear_timer frames (28h before the first)
name DATA:8AB7 rect_clear_timer
name DATA:8A83 done_light_group
comment DATA:8A83 a light group all lit: it blinks for light_group_timer (46h) frames, then goes out (blink_light_group)
name DATA:8A81 light_group_timer
name DATA:8A9D random_lit
comment DATA:8A9D a random light blinks (pick_random_light)
name DATA:8ABE flipper_pressed
comment DATA:8ABE 80h: a flipper key went down (flipper_move), for rotate_lights
name DATA:65A7 lamp_stack
comment DATA:65A7 ign_timers' list of the lit lamps of a group
name DATA:655D jackpot_shown
comment DATA:655D the jackpot as the texts show it (update_texts), copied when it changes
name DATA:6565 hurry_base
name DATA:656D hurry_value
comment DATA:656D the hurry-up's value (8 bytes BCD): hurry_base when armed, + hurry_step every frame (td_hurry)
name DATA:6575 hurry_step
name DATA:6627 roulette_on
name DATA:6628 roulette_pos
name DATA:662A roulette_delay
name DATA:662C roulette_period
name DATA:89B7 always_0
comment DATA:89B7 never written: handlers end with CMP [always_0],0 to return ZF (done), show_text with always_ff to return NZ (go on)
name DATA:6581 always_ff
name DATA:89B8 attract_mode
comment DATA:89B8 FFh while no game runs: lamps with flag 4 blink as well, blinking in every group (blink_lights, update_lights)
name DATA:89B5 booster_col
comment DATA:89B5 where count_boosters writes the boosters into td_txt_boosters
name DATA:9789 lock2_used
comment DATA:9789 set by lock_ball2 (lock3_used by lock_ball3), cleared by new_game, read nowhere
name DATA:978B lock3_used
name DATA:8D88 lights
comment DATA:8D88 light_count records of 26h bytes (the layout of ball_obj): +22h the palette slot (0..), set by init_lights; a lamp's +4 points at one
comment DATA:8AB9 an object whose handler runs every frame until it returns ZF set
name DATA:8A8D ball_locked
name DATA:8A8E locks_lit
name DATA:89C1 light_count
name DATA:89C3 lights_off_pal
name DATA:89C5 lights_on_pal
name DATA:89C7 light_palette
comment DATA:89C7 3 bytes a light: the colours uploaded to DAC 40h.. every tick (upload_lights); a light is on or off by its colours
name DATA:8CEA table_palette
name CODE:3030 test_hit_rects
name CODE:302E hit_sounds
comment CODE:302E test_hit_rects: the hit rectangle's group's sound and jingle word (+2), kept here until a target of it is found
name DATA:8AC1 score_text
comment DATA:8AC1 display_frame: the entry of td_score_texts shown now (the texts that come after a while without score)
name DATA:6DBF txt_count2
comment DATA:6DBF Ignition's text whose +5, +6 update_texts sets to the two digits of the player's second count (record +10h, BCD)
comment CODE:3030 hit_x/hit_y against the hit rectangles, then the targets of the rectangle's group: the first target hit and not yet hit by the player gives hit_object and hit_score (the group), and the group's sounds
comment CODE:3030 a hit rectangle: 0Ah bytes, x1, y1, x2, y2 (inclusive), the group
comment CODE:3030 a group: 16h bytes, +0 its first member (target or lamp), +2 sound (high byte) and jingle (FFh: none), +4 points (BCD, 8 bytes) to the score, +0Ch points to the bonus, +14h a sequence (run_object_event); light groups go on: +16h frames to the next blink, +17h the blink period, +18h the chase phase (blink_lights)
comment CODE:3030 a target: 0Eh bytes, +0 type (1, 8: lit by a hit, mark_hit_object; 4: nothing; 7: a hit then ignored for 14h frames, the count at +0Eh), +1 the players who hit it (a bit each), +2 the lamp lit by a hit (light_hit_object), +4 the next target of the group, +6 x1, +8 y1, +0Ah x2, +0Ch y2 (inclusive)
name CODE:30F3 test_lanes_a
comment CODE:30F3 hit_x/hit_y in a lane (0Ah bytes: x1, y1, x2, y2 (x2, y2 not inside), an object): hit_object = the object, hit_score = its group (+4), hit_lane set, sound 2 (lanes_b: 6); not when tilted
comment CODE:30F3 the lanes' and holes' objects: +0 type, +1 busy/hit bits, +2 a lamp, +4 the group (score, sounds, sequence)
name CODE:30EB test_lanes_b
name CODE:313F light_hit_object
comment CODE:313F the lamp of hit_object (+2) lit for the player
name CODE:315A mark_hit_object
comment CODE:315A hit_object of type 1 or 8: its bit for the player set; type 7: its hit timer (+0Eh) := 14h
name CODE:3192 add_hit_score
comment CODE:3192 the score record's points (+4) to the score, (+0Ch) to the bonus; repeated for a while when a spinner-like object set 8A90h
name CODE:31E4 map_event_run
comment CODE:31E4 AL = map_event + 1: the hole map_events[map_event]: the group's sounds; unless busy (+1): type 6 (a lock: held when the locks are lit), type 5 (the ball held while the group's points are given +8 times, every +6 frames: add_hit_score), both then put the ball at +0Eh, +10h (pixels) with the speed +0Ah, +0Ch and run the group's sequence; type 14h runs the group's sequence; any other just gives hit_object and hit_score; the other holes' busy bytes are cleared
name CODE:3385 run_events
comment CODE:3385 pops the event stack, an entry (0 or FFFFh, an event object) a call; while running_object is set its handler runs instead
comment CODE:3385 FFFFh (armed): sound +1Ch, lamp +1Eh lit (unless +1 = FEh), message +20h (priority +3), flag 4: the timer restarts
comment CODE:3385 0 (fired): points +6 to the score and +0Eh to the bonus (BCD, 8 bytes each), sound +4, count_object, lamp +18h lit, lamp +1Eh out, flag 1: the handler +16h runs every frame until it returns ZF (running_object), flag 2: the timer restarts, the handler +16h, message +1Ah (priority +2)
comment CODE:3385 an event object: 2Ah bytes, +0 type (1Eh: fires only when armed for the player, then disarmed unless +1 = FEh; 1Fh: always), +22h the players it is armed for, +23h flags, +24h the timer's period, +26h the timer (object_timers: at 0 disarmed and lamp +1Eh out); objects with the handler advance_object have 2Eh bytes (+28h, +2Ah, +2Ch)
name CODE:3A0E run_object_event
comment CODE:3A0E SI = a group: its sequence (+14h), if any
name CODE:3A25 run_event
comment CODE:3A25 DI = a sequence: pushes event objects to the event stack; a word of it: an event object, +8000h: arm it (FFFFh on the stack), +4000h: run that sequence instead
comment CODE:3A25 type 2Ah (a word): the words from +2 up to FFFFh, all of them; types 28h, 29h: +2..+9 the step of each player, the step's word at +0Ah + 2 * step: FFFFh nothing, FFFEh step 0 again, FFFDh one step back, FFFCh the step := the next word; type 28h moves one step on after each (back again when an object of type 1Eh is not armed), 29h only by advance_object
name CODE:423C score_object
comment CODE:423C the object's points: +6 to the score, +0Eh to the bonus
name CODE:34A9 set_message
comment CODE:34A9 CX = a message: shown if its priority (DI +2) is not below the running one's
name CODE:34C0 restart_timer
comment CODE:34C0 the object's timer (+26h) := its period (+24h)
name CODE:34C7 count_object
comment CODE:34C7 counts the hits of td_count_obj and td_count_obj2 in the player's record
name CODE:352C blink_lights
comment CODE:352C each light group every +17h frames: lamps with flag 40h change their blink phase, with 20h the group's chase moves a lamp on
name CODE:358E update_lights
comment CODE:358E the current player's lamps into the palette, at most ten changes a frame; player record +18h.. keeps what each lamp shows
comment CODE:358E a lamp: 8 bytes, +0 flags, +1 lit, a bit per player, +2 the blink phase, +3 the state shown with flag 2, +4 the light (palette slot), +6 the next lamp of the group
comment CODE:358E flags: 2 shows +3 (random_light_check, blink_light_group), 4 blinks (unlit; lit too with 10h), 8 not counted by light_group_done, 10h lit means blinking, 20h a chase in the group, 40h blinks, 80h kept at a new ball (lights_off_player)
name CODE:3625 idle_update_lights
name CODE:41B8 light_on
comment CODE:41B8 SI = a light: its palette slot gets the "on" colours
name CODE:41E9 light_off
name CODE:421A upload_lights
comment CODE:421A light_palette to the DAC from colour 40h; the frame callback once the game runs
name CODE:3678 ign_timers
comment CODE:3678 Ignition only: timed lights (td_ign_timers)
name CODE:3722 light_chains
comment CODE:3722 td_chains' groups: the first lamp not lit blinks, the ones after it cleared
name CODE:3766 rect_group_done
comment CODE:3766 all objects of a hit rectangle group lit: its event, then they go out one by one (clear_rect_group)
name CODE:37A9 light_group_done
comment CODE:37A9 a light group (td_lights) with every lamp lit for the player (flag 8 lamps excepted): its sequence runs, the lamps go out and the group blinks (blink_light_group)
name CODE:3805 clear_rect_group
comment CODE:3805 the targets of a completed hit rectangle group go out one by one (rect_clear_target)
name CODE:3831 blink_light_group
comment CODE:3831 the completed light group (done_light_group) blinks, 4-frame phases, until light_group_timer runs out
name CODE:3880 rotate_lights
comment CODE:3880 a flipper was pressed: the lit states of each group of td_rotating move by one (lane change)
name CODE:38BB object_timers7
comment CODE:38BB the hit timers (+0Eh) of the type 7 targets of the level's hit rectangles count down
name CODE:38EB hold_ball_check
comment CODE:38EB a ball in a hole of type 6 or taken by a lock stays held while a message or the events it started run; then it goes (sound 8)
name CODE:2BD9 object_timers
comment CODE:2BD9 td_timed: each running timer (+26h) counts down; at 0 the object is disarmed for the player; its lamp +1Eh goes out while the timer is not running
name CODE:2C11 clear_object_timers
comment CODE:2C11 td_timed's timers stopped
name CODE:2901 reset_locks
comment CODE:2901 each lock empty, its lamp's flags 14h cleared
name CODE:2921 lights_off_player
comment CODE:2921 the player's bits of every lamp cleared, but lamps with flag 80h; the flags 2 cleared
name CODE:294E lights_off_all
comment CODE:294E every lamp out for every player, flags 2 cleared
name CODE:2972 reset_objects
comment CODE:2972 at a new ball: event objects not kept (+1 = 0) disarmed (type 1Fh: armed for all), timers stopped; the sequences of td_events (not kept, not type 2Ah) back to step 0
name CODE:29D2 reset_objects_all
comment CODE:29D2 at a new game: as reset_objects for every object and sequence, kept or not
name CODE:2A6D restore_lights
comment CODE:2A6D at a new ball (reset_ball): the lights' palette from the off colours, then the current player's lit lamps on
name CODE:27E5 reset_targets
comment CODE:27E5 the player's bits of every target of both levels' hit rectangles cleared
name CODE:27F4 reset_rect_targets
comment CODE:27F4 DI = hit rectangles: the player's bit of each target of their groups cleared (lights_frame after types 1, 8)
name CODE:27D5 unused_27D5
comment CODE:27D5 not reached: sixteen INC AX in front of reset_targets
name CODE:2B8E clear_hit
comment CODE:2B8E hit_score, hit_object, hit_x/hit_y and hit_lane cleared, unless the ball is held
name CODE:3308 pick_random_light
comment CODE:3308 one of td_random_lights (frame_count AND 7, the list repeated) gets its lamp blinking (flag 2)
name CODE:3334 random_light_check
comment CODE:3334 while a random light blinks: toggles the blink; a lamp of the list lit (its target hit): if it was the blinking one, td_random_event's sequence; then all stop blinking
name CODE:4328 table_ball_events
comment CODE:4328 per table at a new ball (Steel Wheel, Nightmare: an event)
name CODE:4365 table_game_objects
comment CODE:4365 per table at a new game (Nightmare: the object at 30A6h armed for all)

; object handlers (+16h of an object; coderanges 3C4D-3F99, 4162-41B2)
name CODE:3C40 extra_ball_award
name CODE:3BD3 advance_object
comment CODE:3BD3 a handler (2Eh-byte objects): the sequence +28h one step on for the player (not onto a negative word), the first lamp not lit of the light group +2Ah lit (not with flag 8), the Ignition timer +2Ch restarted (+0 := +2)
name CODE:3C4D obj_nop1
comment CODE:3C4D handlers that do nothing (obj_nop1..6)
name CODE:3C4E obj_nop2
name CODE:3C4F obj_nop3
name CODE:3C50 obj_nop4
name CODE:3D78 obj_nop5
name CODE:3D79 obj_nop6
name CODE:3C51 lock_jackpot
comment CODE:3C51 the jackpot to the score, once more for each of the first two locks that is full (as meant), the count ("n x") into td_txt_jackpot4, the jackpot back to jackpot_base, the locks emptied
comment CODE:3C51 the test of a lock reads [BX+974Eh] (974Eh happens to be map_flags' address; kept a number) where [BX+4] (the lock's state) must have been meant (a bug, presumably): only Nightmare's objects use this handler, and there the first test reads BSS:44CCh, a byte of TBLDETLO.NTM (9Dh: always counted), the second one BSS:44D2h, past the end of that file (memory not loaded; not checked what it holds)
name CODE:3CD8 mult_2
name CODE:3CDE mult_3
name CODE:3CE4 mult_4
name CODE:3CEA mult_5
name CODE:3CF0 mult_6
name CODE:3CF6 mult_7
name CODE:3CFC mult_8
name CODE:3D02 mult_9
name CODE:3D08 mult_10
name CODE:3D0E add_hurry_value
comment CODE:3D0E hurry_value to the score
name CODE:3D1C score_to_best
comment CODE:3D1C adds the current player's score to the best other player's that is not lower (as the code reads; not checked)
name CODE:3D7A nightmare_switch
comment CODE:3D7A jingle 11h, the object at 30A6h armed and the one at 3078h disarmed for the player
name DATA:3078 switch_object_3
comment DATA:3078 the event object nightmare_switch disarms for the player
name CODE:3D93 double_score
comment CODE:3D93 the score doubled
name DATA:8C95 double_tmp
comment DATA:8C95 double_score, double_bonus: a copy of the score or bonus (8 bytes BCD) added to it
name CODE:3DAE double_bonus
comment CODE:3DAE the bonus doubled
name CODE:3DCB hold_bonus
name CODE:3DD1 count_message
comment CODE:3DD1 the message of td_count_texts for the count (player record +16h)
name CODE:3DEC collect_jackpot
comment CODE:3DEC the jackpot to the score, then back to jackpot_base
name CODE:3E23 raise_jackpot
comment CODE:3E23 jackpot += jackpot_step
name CODE:3E47 roulette
comment CODE:3E47 "russian roulette": runs through td_roulette slowing down, lighting each; the last one's event (the start from td_roulette_pick by the frame counter)
name CODE:3F29 countdown
comment CODE:3F29 a handler: the bonus counted into the score now (td_txt_countdown), then waits
name CODE:410C light_locks
comment CODE:410C unless a ball is locked: locks_lit, each lock's lamp lit and blinking (flags 14h)
name CODE:413F lock_ball
comment CODE:413F locks lit: the ball is held, a new one comes (state 4); the two after it the same with 9789h/978Bh set
name CODE:4162 lock_ball2
name CODE:418B lock_ball3

; ---- sound (INT 66h driver)
name CODE:4F50 load_sound_driver
comment CODE:4F50 drive C:, \DELUXE, SOUND.CFG names the driver, EXEC of it, back to the drive it came from
name CODE:510C start_music
comment CODE:510C the table's module (LEVELn.MOD) loaded by the driver, the callbacks timer_callback and module_callback set
name CODE:51A7 stop_sound
comment CODE:51A7 the driver stopped (INT 66h AL=0), no frame callback
name CODE:51C7 module_callback
comment CODE:51C7 the driver's call at the end of a module pattern (presumably): after jingle 6 the main tune again, after 5 tune 0; else the position of the tune playing
name CODE:5201 timer_callback
comment CODE:5201 each tick of the driver's timer: the sprites (sprites_in_irq), the frame callback, the music and sound requests, timer_tick
name CODE:52F8 music_volume_step
comment CODE:52F8 not called
name CODE:5315 play_tune
comment CODE:5315 the table's main tune (main_tunes) started
name CODE:533E music_fade
comment CODE:533E music_fade_dir 1: the volume up in 10h steps, 2: down, then the main tune (the volume set with INT 66h AL=6)
name CODE:53BE tune_request_run
comment CODE:53BE tune_request: 80h fades out, else that position of the table's tunes (music_files)
name CODE:5410 jingle_request_run
comment CODE:5410 jingle_request: a position of the table's jingle list played (80h: back to the main tune)
name CODE:54AD sound_request_run
comment CODE:54AD sound_request: the effect of the table's list played (INT 66h AL=11h)
name XDATA:0000 jingle_num
comment XDATA:0000 XDATA: the sound routines' data (DS = XDATA there): the jingle playing
name XDATA:0001 music_pos
comment XDATA:0001 the module position last started (INT 66h AL=10h)
name XDATA:0003 tune_playing
comment XDATA:0003 1 after a tune started, 0 while a jingle plays
name XDATA:0005 music_files
comment XDATA:0005 records of 4 bytes, the tables' from the third on (table + 2): the module's file name (LEVELn.MOD, start_music), the positions for tune_request 0 and 1
name XDATA:03A6 jingle_lists
comment XDATA:03A6 per table a list of module positions, by jingle_request (negative: none)
name XDATA:03AE main_tunes
comment XDATA:03AE per table + 2 the position of the main tune (play_tune)
name XDATA:03BA effect_lists
comment XDATA:03BA per table a list of sound effects by sound_request, 4 bytes each: BL, BH, CL, DL of INT 66h AL=11h
name XDATA:03CA deluxe_dir
comment XDATA:03CA "\deluxe", where load_sound_driver finds SOUND.CFG and the drivers
name TDATA:1900 display_dots
comment TDATA:1900 where draw_char writes a character's bytes into video memory: word counts and offsets, per plane (the layout not read in detail)
name TDATA:1AB8 display_font
comment TDATA:1AB8 16 bytes a character: the first for the space, then from '0' (30h) on, in the order of the codes (DL - 2Fh)
name DATA:83AD sound_on
name DATA:83AE timer_tick
name DATA:8453 tune_request
comment DATA:8453 FFh none, 80h fade out, else a position of the module's main tune (presumably)
name DATA:8454 sound_request
comment DATA:8454 a sound effect: FFh none, else an entry of the table's effect list (4 bytes, INT 66h AL=11h)
name DATA:8455 jingle_request
comment DATA:8455 a short tune: FFh none, else an entry of the table's jingle list (a module position)
name DATA:8459 sprites_in_irq
name DATA:845A frame_callback
comment DATA:845A called every tick: nothing (4BE4h) until the game runs, then upload_lights
name CODE:4BE4 no_callback
name DATA:845C unused_845C
comment DATA:845C st_load writes 5208h here, the value it already has; read nowhere
name DATA:844E music_fade_dir

; ---- options (C:\DELUXE\DDPCOPTN.BIN, written by the menu)
name DATA:9A96 opt_balls
comment DATA:9A96 the options, DDPCOPTN.BIN as it is (defaults in load_options): 1 = 3 balls a game (checked), else 5
name DATA:9A97 opt_music
comment DATA:9A97 1: the music follows the game (tunes and jingles), else presumably one tune
name DATA:9A98 opt_palette
comment DATA:9A98 1: grey palettes
name DATA:9A99 opt_slope
comment DATA:9A99 gravity = 9 + 2 * (opt_slope - 1) (presumably the table's slope)
name DATA:9A9A key_lflipper
comment DATA:9A9A the keys, as byte index and mask of key_map: LShift, RShift, Space, E0 Down (checked)
name DATA:9A9C key_rflipper
name DATA:9A9E key_nudge
name DATA:9AA0 key_plunger
name DATA:9AA2 opt_screen
comment DATA:9AA2 1: 320x200, 2: 320x350, the table scrolls less (checked with a DDPCOPTN.BIN of 14 bytes); a byte, the file's last: the menu writes 13 bytes and takes no other size (DDPCMAIN's save_options and load_options), load_file here reads any length, load_options' defaults write a word (9AA3h = 0)
name DATA:845E options_file
name DATA:80BC hiscore_file

; ---- names the C port (port/) needs
name DATA:0058 txt_load_error
comment DATA:0058 fatal_error's text ('$' at its end, for INT 21h AH=9)
name DATA:0083 txt_no_memory
name DATA:00A7 name_flippers
name DATA:8095 name_tbldetlo
comment DATA:8095 the table's file names; load_table_files writes the extension (from table_exts) after the dot
name DATA:80A2 name_tbldethi
name DATA:80B0 name_table2m
name DATA:80D3 table_exts
comment DATA:80D3 the four tables' file name extensions, three letters each
name DATA:8475 cleared_vars
comment DATA:8475 start clears DATA from here up to sprite_seg
name DATA:6735 txt_hiscore1
comment DATA:6735 the table's four high scores as texts for the display (format_hiscores): initials at +0, the score at +5
name DATA:674A txt_hiscore2
name DATA:675F txt_hiscore3
name DATA:6774 txt_hiscore4
name CODE:4F05 crtc_480
comment CODE:4F05 set_mode_e3's CRTC registers (index, value), 10 of them
name CODE:4F19 crtc_350
comment CODE:4F19 set_mode_350's CRTC registers (index, value), 16 of them
name CODE:51FE tune_saved
comment CODE:51FE jingle_request_run: 1 once a jingle (2 and up) has taken the music over and music_pos holds where the tune was
name CODE:5200 in_timer
comment CODE:5200 FFh while timer_callback runs (it does not run twice at once)
name DATA:844F fade_steps
comment DATA:844F music_fade: steps left (10h a fade)
name DATA:8450 fade_volume
comment DATA:8450 music_fade: the volume handed to INT 66h AL=6 (up to 100h)
name DATA:7CE6 sprites_scroll
comment DATA:7CE6 bit 0: draw_sprites calls scroll_step before putting an area back; timer_callback clears it, nothing sets it (as far as the code shows)
name DATA:7CF2 sprite_list_end
comment DATA:7CF2 draw_sprites: one past the last entry of sprite_list
name DATA:7CF4 area_offset
comment DATA:7CF4 draw_sprites: the area's first line in video memory (780h + 50h a line)
name DATA:7CF6 area_rows
comment DATA:7CF6 draw_sprites: the area's lines above line 512
name DATA:7CF8 sprite_list
comment DATA:7CF8 draw_sprites: the sprites (their offsets in sprites) of one area, a word each, sorted downwards
